---
import CortexInfoLayout from '../../layouts/CortexInfoLayout.astro';
import { COMPANY } from '../../data/apps';

const supportHref = `mailto:${COMPANY.email}?subject=Cortex%20Support`;
---

<CortexInfoLayout
  title={`Cortex Support - ${COMPANY.name}`}
  description="Help with Cortex for iPhone and iPad, including Game Center, saved progress, iCloud, sound, haptics, and accessibility."
  path="/cortex/support"
  heading="Cortex Support"
  intro="Quick help for Cortex, the local-first iOS hub for Sudoku, word games, logic puzzles, and arcade play."
  current="support"
>
  <p class="cx-info-summary">
    Cortex keeps progress and settings on your device. Before troubleshooting saved
    data, <strong>do not delete the app</strong>: deleting Cortex also removes its
    locally stored data.
  </p>

  <nav class="cx-info-topic-nav" aria-label="Support topics">
    <p>Jump to a topic</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#game-center">Game Center</a></li>
      <li><a href="#saved-progress">Saved progress and iCloud</a></li>
      <li><a href="#sound-haptics">Sound and haptics</a></li>
      <li><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></li>
      <li><a href="#contact">Contact Nintek</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <section aria-labelledby="game-center">
    <h2 id="game-center">Game Center</h2>
    <p>If scores, leaderboards, or achievements are not updating:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Open Apple Settings, search for Game Center, and confirm that Game Center is
        enabled and signed in to the Apple Account you intend to use.
      </li>
      <li>
        Confirm that the device has an internet connection. Cortex itself is
        local-first, but Game Center needs a connection to communicate with Apple.
      </li>
      <li>
        Reopen Cortex and complete another scored game or achievement action. Apple
        updates may take a short time to appear.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="saved-progress">
    <h2 id="saved-progress">Saved progress and iCloud</h2>
    <p>
      Gameplay progress, settings, and detailed play statistics are stored locally.
      If something appears missing, fully close and reopen Cortex on the same device
      before changing anything else. Do not delete the app: deletion removes its local
      data. If iOS has offloaded Cortex, tap its icon to reinstall it; offloading
      preserves the app's documents and data.
    </p>
    <p>
      Sudoku may use Apple's iCloud key-value storage for sync. For Sudoku sync,
      confirm that both devices use the same Apple Account, iCloud is enabled, and
      each device has an internet connection. Open Sudoku on each device and allow a
      moment for Apple to synchronize the data.
    </p>
    <p class="cx-info-note">
      <strong>Important:</strong> Nintek has no Cortex backend and cannot retrieve a
      deleted local save. Deleting Cortex should be a last resort.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="sound-haptics">
    <h2 id="sound-haptics">Sound and haptics</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Check the sound and haptic preferences inside Cortex.</li>
      <li>Raise the device's media volume and check whether Silent Mode is enabled.</li>
      <li>
        In Apple Settings, search for Sounds &amp; Haptics and confirm that system
        haptics are allowed.
      </li>
      <li>
        Keep in mind that the available haptic feedback can vary by game and device.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="accessibility">
    <h2 id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      If an iOS accessibility setting is not behaving as expected, confirm the
      setting under Apple Settings &gt; Accessibility, then fully close and reopen
      Cortex. When reporting an issue with VoiceOver, larger text, Reduce Motion, or
      another accessibility feature, include the game and screen where it occurs so
      it can be reproduced directly.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="contact">
    <h2 id="contact">Contact Nintek</h2>
    <p>
      Still need help? Email Nintek and include your device model, iOS version,
      Cortex version, the game you were using, and what you expected to happen. Do
      not include your Apple Account password or other sensitive account details.
    </p>
    <p class="cx-info-contact">
      <a href={supportHref}>Email {COMPANY.email}</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      For details about local data and Apple services, read the
      <a href="/cortex/privacy">Cortex Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</CortexInfoLayout>
